# image-decoders.plan — the `image.Decode` registry wiring and the two gates that decide which
# uploads this server answers, 2026-09-20. See MIGRATION.md "The remaining image decoders".
#
# `pkg` lines run goimage's own tests (MUTATE_PACKAGE=goimage, no stack); `unit` lines run the
# mm-app lib tests; `api` lines run parity::image_uploads against the Go server on the stack.
#
# Two kinds of decision are under test here and they fail in opposite directions. A registry arm
# that names the wrong decoder or the wrong format string produces a WRONG ANSWER. A gate that
# lists the wrong formats produces a wrong *forward*: too few and the server answers something it
# cannot reproduce, too many and it hands Go work it could have done — the second is invisible to
# every test that only compares served answers, which is why `the_undecoded_formats_still_forward`
# exists.
